% lib/lomo.le — the words of LOMO, the Legal Obligation Metadata Ontology of
% the European institutions (http://data.europa.eu/leg/lomo, version 1.1.0),
% and what the statements of a LOMO description mean together.
%
% A library, not syntax. The LOMO translator (migration/lomo/) turns each
% LOMO description (a Turtle file) into a program of facts, the *register*,
% which includes this library as a resource. One fact of the register is one
% statement of the description:
%
%     norm publication obligation is a substantive rule.
%     norm publication obligation has the modality obligation.
%     norm publication obligation is established in "http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2013/34/art_30/par_1/oj".
%     step publish full report has the agent role agent role micro undertaking publisher.
%
% The library says once what every register means: the kinds of rule, the
% links read in both directions, who acts in which role, the acts and
% articles of the provisions. The questions of LOMO's requirements document
% are queries of each register (the translator writes them).
%
% A LOMO description has no conditions and no cases. So this library does
% not decide whether a rule applies to a case; the parts of it that do
% (deadlines, who is bound, derogation, the conditions of a rule) are below,
% in their own sections.
%
% LOMO is published by the European Union under the Creative Commons
% Attribution 4.0 licence. This library is part of Logical English
% (Apache License 2.0); it was not written or reviewed by the makers of LOMO.

the knowledge base lomo includes these resources:
    lomo.pl.

the functions are:
    the act of *a provision* is *an act*.
    the place of *a provision* in its act is *a text*.

