the knowledge base lomo includes:

% ---- the kinds of rule (LOMO's classes and subclasses) -------------------

a thing is a legal rule if the thing is a prescriptive rule.
a thing is a legal rule if the thing is a constitutive rule.
a thing is a prescriptive rule if the thing is a substantive rule.
a thing is a prescriptive rule if the thing is an implementation and oversight rule.
a thing is a constitutive rule if the thing is a definition.
a thing is a constitutive rule if the thing is a scope rule.
a thing is a constitutive rule if the thing is an institutional rule.

a thing is an agent or agent type if the thing is an agent.
a thing is an agent or agent type if the thing is an agent type.

% Every kind of thing a description names, as one sentence: "which thing
% is of which kind" lists the things of a description.

a thing is of the kind legal rule if the thing is a legal rule.
a thing is of the kind prescriptive rule if the thing is a prescriptive rule.
a thing is of the kind substantive rule if the thing is a substantive rule.
a thing is of the kind implementation and oversight rule if the thing is an implementation and oversight rule.
a thing is of the kind constitutive rule if the thing is a constitutive rule.
a thing is of the kind definition if the thing is a definition.
a thing is of the kind scope rule if the thing is a scope rule.
a thing is of the kind institutional rule if the thing is an institutional rule.
a thing is of the kind action if the thing is an action.
a thing is of the kind agent if the thing is an agent.
a thing is of the kind agent type if the thing is an agent type.
a thing is of the kind agent role if the thing is an agent role.
a thing is of the kind temporal specification if the thing is a temporal specification.
a thing is of the kind action result if the thing is an action result.
a thing is of the kind action result type if the thing is an action result type.
a thing is of the kind legal condition if the thing is a legal condition.
a thing is of the kind process if the thing is a process.
a thing is of the kind dataset if the thing is a dataset.
a thing is of the kind standard if the thing is a standard.
a thing is of the kind software if the thing is a software.
a thing is of the kind public service if the thing is a public service.
a thing is of the kind assessment if the thing is an assessment.
a thing is of the kind assessment statement if the thing is an assessment statement.
a thing is of the kind concept if the thing is a concept.
a thing is of the kind concept scheme if the thing is a concept scheme.

% ---- the links, read in both directions -----------------------------------
% A description may state a link or its opposite (LOMO declares both). The
% sentences below hold whichever of the two was stated.

a rule is a derogation from a second rule if the rule derogates from the second rule.
a rule is a derogation from a second rule if the second rule is derogated by the rule.

a rule is a specification of a second rule if the rule specifies the second rule.
a rule is a specification of a second rule if the second rule is specified by the rule.

a rule is related to a second rule if the rule relates to the second rule.
a rule is related to a second rule if the second rule relates to the rule.

an action comes before a second action if the action is followed by the second action.
an action comes before a second action if the second action follows the action.

a definition gives the meaning of a thing if the definition defines the thing.
a definition gives the meaning of a thing if the thing is defined by the definition.

a dataset holds a result if the dataset manifests the result.
a dataset holds a result if the result is manifested in the dataset.

a definition has the same meaning as a second definition if the definition is equivalent to the second definition.
a definition has the same meaning as a second definition if the second definition is equivalent to the definition.

a temporal specification is the start of a second temporal specification if the temporal specification starts the second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is the start of a second temporal specification if the second temporal specification is started by the temporal specification.

a temporal specification is the end of a second temporal specification if the temporal specification finishes the second temporal specification.
a temporal specification is the end of a second temporal specification if the second temporal specification is finished by the temporal specification.

% ---- agents and their roles -----------------------------------------------
% An action has agent roles; each joins one agent (a named one, or a type of
% agent) to one role: addresser, addressee or beneficiary.

an agent acts as a role in an action if
    the action has the agent role an agent role
    and the agent role is for the agent the agent
    and the agent role has the role the role.

a rule concerns an agent if
    the rule produces an action
    and the agent acts as a role in the action.

a rule has the modality a modality for an agent as a role if
    the rule has the modality the modality
    and the rule produces an action
    and the agent acts as the role in the action.

% ---- time -----------------------------------------------------------------

a thing has a temporal specification as a function if
    the thing has the time specification the temporal specification
    and the temporal specification has the function the function.

% The event that triggers an action or a rule, as the description names it.
a thing is triggered by an event if
    the thing has a temporal specification as trigger
    and the temporal specification has the temporal label the event.

% ---- provisions and acts --------------------------------------------------
% A provision is named by its ELI, the European Legislation Identifier: the
% address of an act, an article, a paragraph or a point. lomo.pl reads the
% act and the place in the act from the address.

a rule is established by the act an act if
    the rule is established in a provision
    and the act of the provision is the act.

a rule is laid down in a place if
    the rule is established in a provision
    and the place of the provision in its act is the place.

a rule is established in more than one provision if
    the rule is established in a provision
    and the rule is established in a second provision
    and the provision is different from the second provision.

% ---- the texts of a thing -------------------------------------------------

a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the label the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the title the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the description the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the comment the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the preferred label the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the explanation the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the legal text the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the temporal label the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the definiendum the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the definiens the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the term label the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the capability the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the purpose the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the judgement the text.
a thing is described by the text a text if the thing has the interpretation the text.

% ---- the word lists of LOMO -----------------------------------------------
% A register writes a term of LOMO's word lists as a word (obligation,
% deadline, addresser, data ...). Their labels, in English, as the word lists
% give them (the authority table of roles of the Publications Office for the
% three roles).

obligation has the preferred label "Obligation".
permission has the preferred label "Permission".
prohibition has the preferred label "Prohibition".
right has the preferred label "Right".
deadline has the preferred label "Deadline".
validity has the preferred label "Validity".
starting point has the preferred label "Starting Point".
trigger has the preferred label "Trigger".
report has the preferred label "Report".
certificate has the preferred label "Certificate".
data has the preferred label "Data".
observation has the preferred label "Observation".
digital public service has the preferred label "Digital Public Service".
digital solutions has the preferred label "Digital Solution".
process automation has the preferred label "Process Automation".
data flow has the preferred label "Data Flow".
